    "body": "## C038 closed: complete neutral P16 clock census\n\nOwner `interactive-reach06-p16-clock-census-20261025-c038` completed HANDOFF-037's bounded diagnostic. [Draft PR #35](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/pull/35) is open, stacked on unchanged draft PR #34.\n\n**Final evidence head:** `30eb22e5df3bc2e70d9af1375cb6b4a8e829724f`  \n**Final evidence tree:** `54be3fad596de24927482c74c8e22fab9e2426b3`  \n**Unchanged held execution candidate:** `4ca73909f861fe4bef9694787473621c1d21c140`, tree `87c949b238055af1ce368c694e1d5683c8aeacde`.\n\n### Established result\n\nExactly one original P16 control followed by one post-failure capture preserved the original end 4 / integer fps 1 / helpers false, tolerances and every cap. Full common receipts match: **100,001 shared operations, 95,640 completed reach operations, all 266 categories, numerical/reader caches, settings, source units/program identity, raw traceback and four complete input inventories**. Both original requests retain failure and exit 1. No elapsed-neutrality or performance claim follows.\n\nThe uniquely bound refused authored pair is **160 → 161**, **31/10 → 78/25 seconds**. All **206 rows** had completed exact parsing and direct binary32 rounding checks. The independent analyzer verifies every actual clock word and exact authored value, complete ordering, boundaries **0/2/3/4**, and maximum shift **3/26,214,400 seconds**, within the actual native float tolerance.\n\nClock-stage work reconciles as **14 sampler + 2,677 row + 160 ordering charges = 2,851**. Entry counters are explicitly source-derived, not logged observations. The downstream independent geometry, endpoint and interval-certificate validation remains unvisited; prior producer stages and initial reader certificate shape/count checks already ran. Retained GLB bytes remain unvalidated input from a failed request. No full-request deficit or P16 pass is inferred.\n\n### Verification and preserved failures\n\n- The two requests retained all **1,986 execution inputs / 442,072,108 bytes** unchanged.\n- Analyzer002 passed **85 neutrality / 243 census assertions**. Analyzer001's parse failure, exact failed source, closed streams and original static-review miss remain preserved. Its one-parenthesis correction did not repeat the product pair.\n- Independent raw/source, mathematics, accounting and narrative reviews passed with corrected scope wording. Final metadata review found no blocking discrepancy.\n- The **73-member archive / 1,536,774 bytes / 3 parts** passed exact hashes, membership, ZIP CRC and fresh extraction.\n- Documentation passed on actual published `920f74f5d83d6e58187b9fb24b8a2a3004daa57a`: **29 sources / 233 sections / 1,485 local links**, zero failures. All **2,117 inputs / 466,811,301 bytes** were stable. The final child only adds closed receipts.\n- All **46 new files / 4,894,817 bytes** match remote Git blob identities. The complete final tree matches all **2,128 local files / 467,811,359 bytes**. Exact original commit objects are hash-verified and the local checkout is clean.\n- GitHub reports **zero Actions runs** for the final head. No full original28, regression or timing cohort was repeated; no hosted/paid job was dispatched.\n\n[HANDOFF-038](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/30eb22e5df3bc2e70d9af1375cb6b4a8e829724f/docs/engineering/reach-recording-validation-2026-10-23/HANDOFF-038.md) · [Census](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/30eb22e5df3bc2e70d9af1375cb6b4a8e829724f/docs/engineering/reach-recording-validation-2026-10-23/checkpoint-038-census.md) · [Complete analysis](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/30eb22e5df3bc2e70d9af1375cb6b4a8e829724f/docs/engineering/reach-recording-validation-2026-10-23/checkpoint-038-analysis.json) · [Manifest](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/30eb22e5df3bc2e70d9af1375cb6b4a8e829724f/docs/engineering/reach-recording-validation-2026-10-23/checkpoint-038-manifest.json) · [Reviews](https://github.com/Omegapy/OntoKin/blob/30eb22e5df3b